From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:03:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] NSP script: hand the extraction and the shader split to
 nxbuild when asked

nxbuild (a build tool in Rust) reproduces the extraction and the shader split
byte for byte and much faster: about 15 s for both versions of Wonder against
2:27 for nx_extract and 0:43 for shader_split.py.

With DM_EXPERIMENTAL_BUILDER=1 and NXB_BIN (the nxb binary or its folder) the
script runs nxb-extract and nxb-split for these stages. It stays the driver:
stage names, events, work folder and reuse keys do not change. A case nxbuild
is not given (XCI, NSZ, merged packages, --program, --allow-damaged, DLC,
captures, NROs, a decoder, a provisional or derived profile), an nxbuild exit
code other than 0 (4 is "not supported yet") and an output that fails the
checks (the title, ExeFS/main, RomFS.img and the marker for an extraction,
the profile's table rows for the split) run the standard step, with a note.
nxbuild's own red lines stay in its log, since the build did not fail.
Without the variable nothing changes.

A Switch 2 package (.nup) goes to nxb-extract --nup (no keys) the same way: the
version's image, ExeFS and control data land in extract/<version>, the DLC
images in aoc/, in the layout pack_nup.py writes. The script keeps its own
reuse key for them (the NUP's size and time, the version, the tool), since
nxb-extract writes no RomFS.img.inputs.json. The checks are ExeFS/main,
RomFS.img, the marker and the '<program ID> version <v>:' line of its log. A
failed or unsupported run, or a failed check, runs pack_nup.py instead.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1325
Reason: the launcher's opt-in experimental builder (nxbuild) runs the extraction (NSP and NUP) and the shader split
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#749
